{
  "note": "One reading of a policy component's verdict, pinned for both implementations (docs/WASM.md D20, W15 review H1). `Ouroboros.Wasm.PolicyEngine.read_verdict/1` and `ouro`'s `wasm_cli::PolicyVerdict::parse` are separate readers of the same untrusted document, and a component that could make them disagree could show an operator one word and hand the node another. `decision` here is the word both must reach; null is `unreadable`, which the node answers as `ask` and the CLI prints as such.",
  "max_document_bytes": 1024,
  "cases": [
    {
      "why": "a verdict is an object with exactly `decision` and `rule`",
      "raw": "{\"decision\":\"deny\",\"rule\":\"no network from a shell\"}",
      "decision": "deny"
    },
    {
      "why": "the other two decisions read the same way",
      "raw": "{\"decision\":\"allow\",\"rule\":\"r\"}",
      "decision": "allow"
    },
    {
